caption: Sanctified Weapons
setting-component: sanctified-weapons

Ordinary sacrificial weapons must be sanctified by a priest of Niktul. Normal sanctification lasts only for the Blood Moon in which it is performed and ends at dawn.

This gives the priesthood practical control over access to valid sacrifice without making ordinary weapons illegal or useless. A gun can still kill someone during the Blood Moon, but it cannot produce a valid sacrifice. Likewise, an unsanctified sword may be lethal but does not deliver the victim to Niktul under the Covenant.

Priests can sanctify their own eligible weapons. More advanced priests can create or enchant permanently sanctified weapons. A permanently sanctified weapon remains eligible for the Hunt without requiring fresh priestly consecration each month; the exact enchanting procedure is not yet defined.

Old permanently sanctified weapons are likely to become important heirlooms, religious relics, and status objects because they represent independent access to the Hunt.
